<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Lanschot ups Nedlloyd to Outperformer.</title>
<headline>Van Lanschot ups Nedlloyd to Outperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (20/06)</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    Nedlloyd	  transport     53.30   Van Lanschot Bankiers</p>
<p>COMMENT: Outperformer (from Market Performer)</p>
<p>First quarter results far worse than expected but company seen heading towards strong turn-around in second half of this year. Cost savings of P&amp;O Nedlloyd estimated at $200 million within 18 months, which larger than previously expected. Cost reductions and planned volume growth will offset pressure on tariffs. Nedlloyd back on track again, we rate the stock as Outperformer for next six to 12 months.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     2.16    24.8   4.0    1.25</p>
<p>    1997		  4.35    12.3   3.8    1.25</p>
<p>    1998		  5.20    10.3   4.5    1.25</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
